# Tests.AnchorsVexSilD — D354 (V9b): the VEX memory forms of the six packed moves, against a processor, FAULT ROWS included

A NEW metered unit (D354 prediction 7), judged once against an absolute registration measured on its own machine
(`scripts/kernel_ceilings.txt`).

The block between the markers is GENERATED by `hwprobe/mk_vexsild_anchors.py` (`--check` gates it byte for byte).

LANE. Personal lane, public sources only.
-/
import X86

namespace X86.Tests.VexSilD
open X86

/-! ## D354 (V9b) — VMOVDQA VMOVDQU VMOVAPS VMOVUPS VMOVAPD VMOVUPD, m128 and m256, loads and stores, against a processor

The value rows also have a differential partner (`Tests.Vectors.vexMovVectors`); the 30 FAULT rows do not, because ACL2
x86isa (and Rosetta 2) execute an aligned kind's misaligned encoding where the SDM says #GP.  For those rows these pins
and `hwprobe/vexsild_probe.c` are the only check that the model faults.

The pre-state is the probe's (`hwprobe/vexsild_ops.S`): YMM1-3, RAX, MXCSR and the flags from the row, the qwords of the
row's 64-byte buffer that the access spans, at `v9bBuf` (32-byte aligned, as the probe's buffer is), and RBX =
`v9bBuf + off`.  A value row agrees when the step did not stop, YMM3 holds the row's 256 bits, YMM1, YMM2, RAX, MXCSR and
the six flags are unchanged, RIP moved by the instruction's length, and the spanned qwords hold the row's expected bytes
(a store's 16 or 32 bytes and their neighbours inside those qwords).  A fault row agrees when the step stopped `byDesign`
and the spanned qwords are unchanged. -/

private def v9bFlags (f : BitVec 64) : Flags :=
  ⟨f.getLsbD 0, f.getLsbD 2, f.getLsbD 4, f.getLsbD 6, f.getLsbD 7, f.getLsbD 11, false⟩

private def v9bRflags (f : Flags) : BitVec 64 :=
  flagFields.foldl (fun acc r => acc ||| (if r.get f then (1 : BitVec 64) <<< r.bit else 0)) 0

private def v9bSetYmm (c : Cpu) (r : XmmReg) (y : BitVec 256) : Cpu :=
  let c := c.setXmm r (y.setWidth 128)
  { c with xmm := { c.xmm with hi := c.xmm.hi.set r ((y >>> 128).setWidth 128) } }

private def v9bYmm (t : Cpu) (r : XmmReg) : BitVec 256 :=
  ((t.getYmmHi r).setWidth 256 <<< 128) ||| (t.getXmm r).setWidth 256

/-- Where the row's buffer lives in the model's memory: 32-byte aligned, so a row's alignment is its offset's. -/
private def v9bBuf : BitVec 64 := 0x10000

private def v9bPre (y1 y2 y3 : BitVec 256) (f : BitVec 64) (mx : BitVec 32) (rax : BitVec 64) (mem : List (Nat × BitVec 64))
    (off : BitVec 64) : Cpu :=
  let c := (v9bSetYmm (v9bSetYmm (v9bSetYmm ({ flags := v9bFlags f, rip := 0x400000, mxcsr := mx, oracle := Oracle.zero }
    : Cpu) .x1 y1) .x2 y2) .x3 y3).setReg .q .rax rax
  let c := mem.foldl (fun c (j, q) => c.writeMem .q (v9bBuf + BitVec.ofNat 64 (8 * j)) q) c
  c.setReg .q .rbx (v9bBuf + off)

private def v9bStoppedByDesign (t : Cpu) : Bool :=
  match t.ms with
  | some (.byDesign _) => true
  | _ => false

private def v9bAgrees (t : Cpu) (n : Nat) (y1 y2 : BitVec 256) (f : BitVec 64) (mx : BitVec 32) (rax : BitVec 64)
    (fault : Bool) (w3 : BitVec 256) (wmem : List (Nat × BitVec 64)) : Bool :=
  (if fault then v9bStoppedByDesign t
   else t.ms.isNone && v9bYmm t .x3 == w3 && v9bYmm t .x1 == y1 && v9bYmm t .x2 == y2
     && t.getReg .q .rax == rax && t.mxcsr == mx
     && (v9bRflags t.flags &&& 0x8d5) == (f &&& 0x8d5) && t.rip == 0x400000 + BitVec.ofNat 64 n)
  && wmem.all (fun (j, q) => t.readMem .q (v9bBuf + BitVec.ofNat 64 (8 * j)) == q)

